WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.568
-Our first guest
is an Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.670
starring in the hit series
"WandaVision,"

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.139
which is available
on Disney Plus.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.575
Here is Kathryn Hahn!

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.844
Kathryn Hahn! Ah, look.

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.412
Come on, now.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.681
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:18.752
Kathryn, welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.820
I appreciate you being here.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.690
-I am so happy to be back,
my friend.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.791
How are you doing?
-You are the best.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.792
I'm fantastic.
I'm happy to see you.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.260
Mwah, mwah, mwah.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.163
I wanted to thank you for --
for doing that bit with us.

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:33.999
We did "FallonVision,"
the spoofing "WandaVision."

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:36.569
You were so great.
Thank you for doing that.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.838
I --
-How good was that whole thing?!

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.307
I'm so impressed!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.043
And Lizzie? It was so good!

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:47.881
And Lizzie did it from her,
like, hotel room or whatever?

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.383
-Yeah, she was in London.
Elizabeth was in London.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.619
I don't know where you were, but
last time you were on our show,

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.287
by the way, you were nice to me.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:57.356
You came on our show when
we were doing the show from home

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.025
and no one knew
what was going on.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.093
And thank you for doing that.
-Yes.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.028
-I believe you were
in your garage.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.630
-No, I was in my un-air --
yes, a very hot,

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.398
un-air-conditioned garage,

00:01:06.398 --> 00:01:10.870
and I thought I had done it okay
with a self-style.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.906
And then after
the segment aired,

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:18.244
I saw -- I started to get texts
from pals being like,

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:21.047
"Honey, what -- what's --
what happened to your hair?"

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.415
And then when I looked
at it again,

00:01:23.415 --> 00:01:24.683
it really did look like my hair

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:27.353
got caught in a ceiling fan
from behind.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.922
So, clearly, I can't
do my own hair, you guys.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:31.891
It was a rat's nest.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:36.729
-I don't know if this is
that bad, to be honest.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.230
-Oh, come on!

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.733
-No, I think it's --

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.635
I think you look pretty --

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:45.004
I think you look --

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.973
I think you look gorgeous.
-That's very kind.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:50.442
It looks like a horse tail.
That is very, very kind.

00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:53.579
You and --
I remember David Spade was on,

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:54.947
and you and Spade
were yukking it up.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.516
And as the humidity
was happening,

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.685
my hair just kept going like
[Groaning]

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:04.891
And then it was like,
"And 5, 4, 3, 2, and disaster."

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.292
-Oh, my God. No, no.
-But it was fun.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.726
We got through it.
-You're a knockout.

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:09.228
You're a knockout, buddy.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.163
-Oh. Tell me more.

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:12.732
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.467
I want to talk to you
about "WandaVision,"

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.837
because it was the biggest hit
in the entire world.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.272
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.173
Couldn't have been bigger,
and we all needed it.

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:22.908
Everyone was at home.
We needed something --

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:25.444
And you're so good.
You couldn't tell me anything.

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:28.314
And we didn't know --
It was all you the whole time.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.483
-I couldn't tell you anything.
And I'm telling you,

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:33.019
it was every single time
I had to do an interview,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.920
it was like I had to say
a silent prayer,

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.424
because Agnes and Agatha
were just a couple letters off.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:41.227
And I just thought, if I slip,
it's going to be --

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.128
It's going to be not fun for me,

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:44.864
for my family, or my legacy.
-But you pulled it off.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.499
You pulled off
the biggest switcheroo ever.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.934
No one saw it coming.
The Internet broke.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.603
It was fantastic to watch.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:53.339
It was a TV moment.
It was a pop culture moment.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.307
What's it like being
in the Marvel Universe

00:02:55.307 --> 00:02:57.943
and having --
being part of that?

00:02:57.943 --> 00:02:59.412
-It's bananas! I --

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.547
I never saw this
in my -- my future.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:05.084
But to be this part
in this -- in this world

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.987
with those delicious humans --
I mean, you know Lizzie.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.988
She's a gem and a half.

00:03:09.988 --> 00:03:12.458
It's been -- It's so fun.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:15.961
Yeah, the best. And to play
a witch? Forget it. The best.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.996
-Yeah. You're getting crazy
awards buzz

00:03:17.996 --> 00:03:20.133
and well -- well-deserved,
as well.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.668
Do your -- Do your kids
think it's cool?

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.570
Are they old enough?

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.939
-I mean, I -- They will
never think I'm cool.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:30.142
Like, I am so embarrassing
to them at all times

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:34.046
to the point that they will
not let me finish a sentence

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.715
without being like,
"Mom, like, please. Don't."

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:39.385
Like, they can't even --
They look at me like

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.821
I can't do anything right
right now.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.189
I mean they're, you know,
teenagers and pre-teenagers.

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:46.192
So I'm not -- you know,
I'm never going to be cool.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.493
-Well, you actually
sent me a thing,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.727
which is very nice of you.

00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:53.265
You sent me a note
that your daughter wrote to you?

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:56.235
-Yeah, this is true.
-Look at this.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:58.671
-That is pretty cute, guys.
This is at the finale.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:01.874
-"Dear Mom, congrats!
You were<i> such</i> a bad-ass.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.876
We love you,
and we're so proud of you.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:06.212 line:0%
XOXO. P.S. Sleep well."

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.413 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.181
Come on. That's not bad.

00:04:09.181 --> 00:04:11.651
-She -- That was after
seeing the finale.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:14.653
So, yes, you're right. That was
very cute, language aside.

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:17.723
In that -- In that letter,
it was appropriate.

00:04:17.723 --> 00:04:19.425
-Language aside, yeah.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:22.628
But also, you got a #1 song
in the iTunes chart

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:24.163
out of "WandaVision."

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.731
"Agatha --"
Someone's going nuts here --

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:30.169
"Agatha All Along" went to #1
on iTunes on the charts

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.670
'cause that was your song
that you sang,

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.306
and you knocked it
out of the park.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.041
Were you nervous to sing it?

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:38.210
-I mean, apparently over Biebs.
I was like, "What is happening?"

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.612
Like, I was --
-Biebs!

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:43.149
-I mean -- The Biebs!
Sorry, Biebs.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:45.518
I can't -- I'm sorry, Biebs.
I can't help you.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:48.654
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:49.922
-You are the best.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:53.826
"Sorry, Biebs,
I can't help you."

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.861
Congrats on the success
of "WandaVision."

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:57.863
You crush it, as you always do.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:05:00.032
I want to show everyone
part of the scene

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.567
featuring the song
"Agatha All Along."

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.503
Here's Kathryn Hahn
in "WandaVision." Take a look.

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:07.940 line:0%
-♪ It's been Agatha all along ♪

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.243 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:13.579 line:0%
-♪ She's insidious ♪
-Ha-ha!

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:16.816
-♪ So perfidious ♪

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:20.252
♪ That you haven't even noticed,
and the pity is ♪

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:21.320
-♪ The pity is ♪

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.988
-♪ Pity, pity, pity, pity ♪

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:26.158 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.961
♪ It's too late
to fix anything ♪

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:32.231
♪ Now that everything
has gone wrong ♪

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.832
♪ Thanks to Agatha ♪
-Ha!

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:35.467
-♪ Naughty Agatha ♪

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:38.604
-♪ It's been Agatha all along ♪

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:41.741
[ Gasps ]
And I killed Sparky, too.

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:43.976
[ Laughing ]

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.145
-Come on, dude!

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:49.515
You were brilliant!
It was so great!

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.317
I love you did that.

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:52.618
Kathryn Hahn, everybody.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.254
Check out "WandaVision"
on Disney Plus.

